    "created_at": "2015-11-23T20:03:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-23T20:03:59Z",
    "body": "annevk,\n\nThanks for your reply. To clarify: I'm not asking for the specification to mandate any particular kind of UI. I'm just asking if the specification can mandate that the browser respect 'autofill off' to _disable_ a UI.\n\nThere are many precedents for this in the spec. For example (emphasis mine):\n\n> A form control that is disabled _must_ prevent any click events\n> The readonly attribute... When specified, the element _is not_ mutable\n> The required attribute... When specified, the element _is_ required\n\nNone of these are 'may' or 'should be' (which is quite sensible, IMHO).\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/159047810/reactions",
